From 71787a8a8ed97b372c9aa314495dea793e693cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kanban: capsule card submitter refuses an owner without this
 core's capsule gates

A capsule-required card's gates (admission probe, single-use rendezvous,
--observation-fd) live in the profile owner. kanban_worker_client reached
whatever owner discovery returned; a named profile is served by the root
multiplexer, so a pinned-core submitter reached a global-core owner with no
capsule gates, which admitted the card and ran an ordinary managed worker
(hub 2026-11-02, run4 of t_01a19a6b4fcce737).

The owner now advertises kanban-capsule-transport-v1. For a card whose board
row requires a capsule (derived exactly as the owner derives it; unreadable
fails closed), the submitter requires that capability AND an owner code_sha
equal to its own code identity, checked via connect_gateway(owner_check=...)
before any ticket, dial or kanban.run. The refusal is final
(kanban_capsule_owner_unsupported, exit 1), not an owner wait. Ordinary
cards are unchanged.
